<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!--
        Correct the order confirmation subject line for net-terms orders.

        THE PROBLEM
        ===========
        Stock Odoo builds the subject of sale.mail_template_sale_confirmation
        by asking the TRANSACTION whether it is pending:

            {{ (object.get_portal_last_transaction().state == 'pending')
               and 'Pending Order' or 'Order' }}

        while the body asks the ORDER:

            <t t-if="object.state == 'sale' or (tx_sudo and tx_sudo.state
                     in ('done', 'authorized'))">has been confirmed.

        For every ordinary provider those two agree, because the transaction
        reaching done is what confirms the order. Pay on Account breaks the
        tie: the order is confirmed while the transaction stays pending on
        purpose, since with net terms no money has moved and marking it done
        would make Odoo post a payment that does not exist (see
        models/payment_transaction.py).

        The result is an email headed "Pending Order" whose body says the
        order has been confirmed. That contradiction is the whole complaint
        this work set out to fix, so confirming the order alone is not
        enough.

        THE FIX
        =======
        Ask the order first, exactly as the body does. "Pending Order" now
        appears only when the order really is unconfirmed AND a payment is
        genuinely outstanding, which is still the correct wording for a
        card customer who abandoned payment midway.

        SCOPE
        =====
        This record deliberately omits noupdate, so the subject is
        re-applied on every module upgrade and stays owned by this file.
        Only the subject is written. The body, and every other field on the
        template, is left alone and remains editable in the UI without
        being overwritten.
    -->
    <record id="sale.mail_template_sale_confirmation" model="mail.template">
        <field name="subject">{{ object.company_id.name }} {{ (object.state != 'sale' and object.get_portal_last_transaction().state == 'pending') and 'Pending Order' or 'Order' }} (Ref {{ object.name or 'n/a' }})</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
